              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 12.13: Geometry of solar eclipse (The sizes and distances are not to scale)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.334,
            0.733,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In areas where the Moon partially blocks out only some regions of the Sun, the observers see a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "partial solar eclipse",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (Fig. 12.13 and Fig. 12.14b)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.392,
            0.735,
            0.524
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "During a total solar eclipse, for a few minutes it turns dark during the day as no sunlight reaches the Earth. Due to the Earth’s rotation and the motion of the Moon in its orbit, the Moon’s shadow moves across the surface of the Earth. Thus, the total solar eclipse is visible only for a few minutes. As the Moon begins to move away from the front of the Sun (Fig. 12.14c), we see a partial solar eclipse and daylight begins to return."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.75,
            0.325,
            0.936,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.75,
                0.325,
                0.936,
                0.475
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_12_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.529,
            0.421,
            0.549
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Safe Viewing of a Solar Eclipse"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.075,
            0.552,
            0.115,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.075,
                0.552,
                0.115,
                0.581
              ],
