              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 12.15: A public solar eclipse viewing organised in Ooty, Tamil Nadu"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.408,
            0.638,
            0.639,
            0.655
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "binoculars, or telescopes."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.406,
            0.66,
            0.733,
            0.753
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Usually, astronomy organisations, such as planetaria and astronomy clubs hold eclipse viewing events during a solar eclipse (Fig. 12.15)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.406,
            0.754,
            0.733,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Participating",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in such events is the best way to observe a solar eclipse since the organisers not only provide specialised eye protection for solar viewing, but also offer scientific explanations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
